---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/compare/omnisend-vs-yotpo-email-sms";
const title = "Omnisend vs Yotpo Email & SMS: Shopify migration decision";
const desc = "Evaluate Omnisend as a replacement for retired Yotpo Email & SMS, with separate cart and checkout acceptance checks and a controlled recovery launch.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Can I choose Yotpo Email & SMS for new recovery?",
    "answer": "No. Yotpo scheduled Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025. Its current SMS notice confirms the dashboard and background services are decommissioned."
  },
  {
    "question": "Is Omnisend an automatic winner?",
    "answer": "It is a replacement candidate named in Yotpo\u2019s migration announcement. Demonstrate identification, stage handoff, purchase exits and required channels in your own setup before choosing it."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can I export my old dashboard now?",
    "answer": "No export availability is established. Inventory retained records and ask the provider about any remaining recovery options. Do not assume missing permission records authorize messaging."
  },
  {
    "question": "What does the $699 example show?",
    "answer": "At 60% gross margin, goods cost $279.60. An 18% code leaves $573.18 revenue and $293.58 gross profit, versus $419.40 at full price: a $125.82 reduction before other costs."
  },
  {
    "question": "When can I enable the new flow?",
    "answer": "After permissions, cart links, purchase exits and competing queues are reconciled. Start with a limited eligible segment and pause if those controls fail."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="py-16"><div class="container"><h1 class="hero-title">{title}</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl">{desc}</p>

<TldrBox picks={[
{label:'Current candidate',tool:'Omnisend',reason:'Evaluate a rebuild using cart and checkout as distinct stages.'},
{label:'Historical service',tool:'Yotpo Email & SMS',reason:'Retired service; use retained records to plan replacement.'},
{label:'Launch gate',tool:'One recovery owner',reason:'Inspect eligibility and queued messages before enabling the replacement.'}
]} />
<article class="prose-shopify mt-12 max-w-4xl">
<h2>Why this is a migration decision</h2>
<p>Yotpo’s <a href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">September 2025 announcement</a> scheduled Email and SMS deprecation for December 31, 2025 and named Omnisend and Attentive as migration partners. Its <a href="https://email-and-sms.yotpo.com/">current SMS notice</a> says dashboard access and background services are decommissioned. Checked November 25, 2026. This retirement does not establish the status or capabilities of Yotpo’s separate reviews and loyalty products.</p>
<table class="data-table"><thead><tr><th>Decision</th><th>Omnisend candidate</th><th>Historical Yotpo Email &amp; SMS</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Recovery workflow</td><td>Demonstrate cart-to-checkout handoff and purchase exits.</td><td>Do not plan a new deployment on the retired service.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Records</td><td>Map retained permissions, exclusions and event fields before import.</td><td>Dashboard export availability is not established.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Budget</td><td>Obtain a current quote for audience, channels and migration work.</td><td>Historic tiers and ratings do not describe a current purchase option.</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
<h2>Verify the cart-to-checkout boundary</h2>
<p><a href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/6659889-abandoned-cart-and-abandoned-checkout-automations">Omnisend’s abandonment documentation</a> distinguishes cart activity from checkout activity and describes purchase exits. Confirm identification before testing. Use an identified test shopper, add a product, begin checkout, then purchase while a reminder waits. Inspect both workflow histories and remaining queues. These are proposed exercises, not tests completed for this page.</p>
<h2>Rebuild eligibility before importing an audience</h2>
<p>Inventory retained email and SMS permissions, opt-outs, customer identifiers, templates and incentive rules. A phone number or historical order alone does not establish permission for a new SMS program. Resolve absent evidence with the responsible owner before release. Keep reviews and loyalty integrations on their own checklist; their presence does not restore the retired messaging service.</p>
<h2>Rehearse the difficult carts</h2>
<p>For a subscription toggle or financing interruption, follow the recovery link through checkout and confirm the intended purchase type survives. For a mixed-size cart, remove an unavailable variant and check both product content and destination. For a bundle or signup offer, verify Shopify coupon combinations and avoid automatically adding a second incentive. For an international shopper, inspect shipping terms, currency and permitted channel timing rather than treating every abandonment as price resistance.</p>
<h2>Assign one recovery owner during cutover</h2>
<p>List every active Shopify, email and SMS automation that can reach the same shopper. Disable competing flows and reconcile queued messages before enabling the replacement. Rehearse a purchase between email and SMS and an unsubscribe before the next step. <a href="https://support.omnisend.com/en/articles/4228254-manage-multiple-abandonment-automations">Omnisend’s multiple-automation guidance</a> helps with internal priorities; cross-provider coordination still requires an explicit check.</p>
<h2>Keep the incentive calculation separate from results</h2>
<p>For an illustrative $699 basket at 60% gross margin, goods cost $279.60. Full-price gross profit is $419.40. An 18% code removes $125.82 from revenue, leaving $573.18 revenue and $293.58 gross profit. Subtract fulfillment, payment, messaging and returns before calling the remainder contribution. This model does not show that either provider caused an incremental order.</p>
<h2>Release and measure</h2>
<p>Authenticate the sender, confirm reply routing, test real event-populated cart links and release a limited eligible cohort. Compare deduplicated orders and contribution over the same window. If using a randomized no-message group, choose its size and duration from expected volume and detectable effect. Keep a pause owner for failed purchase exits, missing permissions or broken destinations. Select Omnisend only when the required workflow and operating cost are demonstrated; compare another current candidate if essential requirements remain unmet.</p>
<p>For a separate SMS replacement decision see <a href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-postscript">Yotpo vs Postscript</a>; for signup and offer handoff see <a href="/compare/yotpo-email-sms-vs-privy">Yotpo vs Privy</a>.</p>
</article>

<FaqSection faqs={faqs} /></div></section></BaseLayout>
